],"id":"gcp.kubernetes.storage","l":"limited","t":"Kubernetes Storage (PersistentVolumes, StorageClasses, snapshots)","x":["StorageClasses (real defaults: standard-rwo, premium-rwo, standard), PersistentVolumeClaims and their auto-provisioned PersistentVolumes are real, enforced objects — a PVC binds to a real PV sized/classed exactly as requested, and is reclaimed when the PVC is deleted. VolumeSnapshots/VolumeSnapshotClasses (the CSI snapshot controller) are not modeled."]},{"a":["projects.locations.clusters.k8s.*.list"],"id":"gcp.kubernetes.object-browser","l":"full","t":"Object Browser (generic Kubernetes resource browser)","x":[]},{"a":["projects.locations.backupPlans.create","projects.locations.backupPlans.list","projects.locations.backupPlans.get","projects.locations.backupPlans.delete","projects.locations.backupPlans.backups.create","projects.locations.backupPlans.backups.list","projects.locations.backupPlans.backups.get","projects.locations.backupPlans.backups.delete"],"id":"gcp.kubernetes.backup","l":"limited","t":"Backup for GKE","x":["Backup plans and on-demand backups are real create/list/get/delete resources (gkebackup.googleapis.com's projects.locations.backupPlans and .backups) that snapshot a cluster's GKE control-plane configuration (node pool shapes, version) at backup time. Not modeled: scheduled/automatic backups (backupSchedule is stored but never fires), actual pod volume data capture, and restore (RestorePlan/Restore) — only on-demand backups of cluster config."]},{"a":["projects.locations.clusters.k8s.configmanagement.*","projects.locations.clusters.k8s.constraints.*"],"id":"gcp.kubernetes.config","l":"limited","t":"Config (Config Sync / Policy Controller / fleet configuration)","x":["Policy Controller is real and enforced: a ConfigManagement object with policyController.enabled=true, plus one or more K8sRequiredLabels constraints, genuinely denies admission (403) to Workloads that don't carry the required labels — see test_gcp_gke_dataplane_core.py's admission tests. Config Sync's git half is stored in the same real shape (spec.git.syncRepo/syncBranch/policyDir) but never fetched: cloning a real external git repository needs real internet egress, which the simulator's 'nothing leaves Vyomi' rule (tests/conformance/test_no_cloud_egress.py) forbids outright — not a modeling gap, a sandboxing one."]},{"a":["projects.locations.clusters.k8s.applications.get"],"id":"gcp.kubernetes.applications","l":"full","t":"Applications","x":[]},{"a":["projects.locations.memberships.create","projects.locations.memberships.list","projects.locations.memberships.get","projects.locations.memberships.delete"],"id":"gcp.kubernetes.fleet-registration","l":"full","t":"Fleet registration (GKE Hub / Anthos)","x":[]},{"a":["projects.locations.clusters.k8s.observability.get"],"id":"gcp.kubernetes.observability","l":"limited","t":"Observability & Cost optimization","x":["Resource inventory (namespace/workload/pod/service/secret counts) and a requested-vs-allocatable CPU/memory rollup are real numbers derived from objects genuinely stored in the cluster's data plane and its node pools — never a synthetic series. Historical time-series metrics, Cloud Logging-based insights and automated cost-optimization recommendations need real kubelet/cAdvisor telemetry and Cloud Monitoring, which this simulator does not generate for GKE."]},{"a":["projects.locations.operations.list"],"id":"gcp.kubernetes.logs","l":"limited","t":"Logs","x":["Shows the cluster's real GKE control-plane operations (projects.locations.operations: create/delete cluster, create/delete/resize node pool, upgrades) — genuine history, not placeholder rows. Cloud Logging entries (audit logs, container/workload logs) are not generated, since there is no Kubernetes API server or log-ingestion pipeline behind a simulated cluster."]}],"id":"kubernetes","ops":58,"registry_unreachable":[["gcp.kubernetes.cluster.nodes","projects.locations.clusters.k8s.nodes.list"],["gcp.kubernetes.st